#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Isang libreng kursong IBM sa quantum information at computation"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formulations of measurements"
msgstr "Mga matematikal na pormulasyon ng mga sukat"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore biggr Biggr operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore biggr Biggr operatorname */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The lesson begins with two equivalent mathematical descriptions of "
"measurements:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang aralin ay nagsisimula sa dalawang katumbas na matematikal na "
"paglalarawan ng mga sukat:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"General measurements can be described by *collections of matrices*, one for "
"each measurement outcome, in a way that generalizes the description of "
"projective measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga pangkalahatang sukat ay maaaring ilarawan sa pamamagitan ng mga "
"*koleksyon ng mga matris*, isa para sa bawat resulta ng sukat, sa paraang "
"nagpapalawak sa paglalarawan ng mga projective na sukat.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"General measurements can be described as *channels* whose outputs are always"
" classical states (represented by diagonal density matrices).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga pangkalahatang sukat ay maaaring ilarawan bilang mga *channel* na "
"ang mga output ay palaging mga klasikal na estado (kinakatawan ng mga "
"diagonal na density matrix).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll restrict our attention to measurements having *finitely many* possible outcomes.\n"
"Although it is possible to define measurements with infinitely many possible outcomes, they're much less typically encountered in the context of computation and information processing, and they also require some additional mathematics (namely measure theory) to be properly formalized.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ilililmita natin ang ating pansin sa mga sukat na may *tiyak na bilang* ng mga posibleng resulta.\n"
"Bagama't posible ang mga sukat na may walang katapusang bilang ng mga resulta, mas bihira itong makita sa konteksto ng computation at pagpoproseso ng impormasyon, at nangangailangan din ng karagdagang matematika (lalo na ang measure theory) para maayos na mapormal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our initial focus will be on so-called *destructive* measurements, where the output of the measurement is a classical measurement outcome alone — with no specification of the post-measurement quantum state of whatever system was measured.\n"
"Intuitively speaking, we can imagine that such a measurement destroys the quantum system itself, or that the system is immediately discarded once the measurement is made.\n"
"Later in the lesson we'll broaden our view and consider *non-destructive* measurements, where there's both a classical measurement outcome and a post-measurement quantum state of the measured system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ating unang pokus ay sa tinatawag na *mapanirang* (destructive) na mga sukat, kung saan ang output ng sukat ay isang klasikal na resulta lamang — nang walang detalye ng post-measurement na quantum na estado ng sistemang sinukat.\n"
"Sa simpleng salita, maaari nating isipin na winawasak ng ganitong sukat ang quantum system mismo, o kaya'y agad na itinatapon ang sistema pagkatapos ng sukat.\n"
"Mamaya sa aralin, palawakin natin ang ating pananaw at isasaalang-alang ang *hindi mapanirang* (non-destructive) na mga sukat, kung saan mayroon parehong klasikal na resulta at post-measurement na quantum na estado ng sinukat na sistema.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measurements as collections of matrices {#measurements-as-collections-of-"
"matrices}"
msgstr ""
"Mga sukat bilang koleksyon ng mga matris {#measurements-as-collections-of-"
"matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system that is to be measured, and assume for simplicity that the classical state set of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\{0,\\ldots, n-1\\}$ for some positive integer $n,$ so that density matrices representing quantum states of $\\mathsf{X}$ are $n\\times n$ matrices.\n"
"We won't actually have much need to refer to the classical states of $\\mathsf{X},$ but it will be convenient to refer to $n,$ the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"We'll also assume that the possible outcomes of the measurement are the integers $0,\\ldots,m-1$ for some positive integer $m.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na ang $\\mathsf{X}$ ay isang sistema na susukatin, at para sa simplisidad, ipagpalagay na ang klasikal na set ng estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ ay $\\{0,\\ldots, n-1\\}$ para sa ilang positibong integer na $n,$ kaya ang mga density matrix na kumakatawan sa mga quantum na estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ ay mga $n\\times n$ na matris.\n"
"Hindi talaga natin kailangang lubos na sumangguni sa mga klasikal na estado ng $\\mathsf{X},$ ngunit magiging kapaki-pakinabang na tumukoy sa $n,$ ang bilang ng mga klasikal na estado ng $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Ipagpalagay din natin na ang mga posibleng resulta ng sukat ay mga integer na $0,\\ldots,m-1$ para sa ilang positibong integer na $m.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that we're just using these names to keep things simple;\n"
"it's straightforward to generalize everything that follows to other finite sets of classical states and measurement outcomes, renaming them as desired.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ginagamit lang natin ang mga pangalang ito para gawing simple ang mga bagay;\n"
"diretso ang pagpapalawak ng lahat ng susunod sa ibang mga tiyak na set ng mga klasikal na estado at resulta ng sukat, binabago ang kanilang mga pangalan ayon sa nais.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Mga projective na sukat {#projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that a *projective measurement* is described by a collection of *projection matrices* that sum to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols,\n"
msgstr ""
"Alalahanin na ang isang *projective na sukat* ay inilarawan ng koleksyon ng mga *projection matrix* na ang kabuuan ay katumbas ng identity matrix.\n"
"Sa simbolo,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"describes a projective measurement of $\\mathsf{X}$ if each $\\Pi_a$ is an "
"$n\\times n$ projection matrix and the following condition is met.\n"
msgstr ""
"ay naglalarawan ng isang projective na sukat ng $\\mathsf{X}$ kung ang bawat"
" $\\Pi_a$ ay isang $n\\times n$ na projection matrix at natutupad ang "
"sumusunod na kondisyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it's in a state described by some quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ each outcome $a$ is obtained with probability equal to $\\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.$\n"
"We also have that the post-measurement state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is obtained by normalizing the vector $\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ but we're ignoring the post-measurement state for now.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag ginanap ang ganitong sukat sa isang sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ habang ito ay nasa isang estado na inilarawan ng ilang quantum state vector na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ ang bawat resulta na $a$ ay nakukuha nang may probabilidad na katumbas ng $\\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.$\n"
"Mayroon din tayong post-measurement na estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ na nakukuha sa pamamagitan ng pag-normalize ng vector na $\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ ngunit binabalewala natin ang post-measurement na estado sa ngayon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is described by a density matrix $\\rho$ "
"rather than a quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ then we can "
"alternatively express the probability to obtain the outcome $a$ as "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ ay inilarawan ng isang density matrix na "
"$\\rho$ sa halip na isang quantum state vector na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ "
"maaari nating alternatibong ipahayag ang probabilidad na makuha ang resulta "
"na $a$ bilang $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $\\rho = \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ is a pure state, then "
"the two expressions are equal:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang $\\rho = \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ ay isang pure "
"state, ang dalawang expression ay pantay:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi \\vert)\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi \\vert)\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're using the cyclic property of the trace for the second equality, "
"and for the third equality we're using the fact that each $\\Pi_a$ is a "
"projection matrix, and therefore satisfies $\\Pi_a^2 = \\Pi_a.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito ginagamit natin ang cyclic property ng trace para sa ikalawang "
"pagkakapantay, at para sa ikatlong pagkakapantay ginagamit natin ang "
"katotohanan na ang bawat $\\Pi_a$ ay isang projection matrix, at samakatuwid"
" ay nakakatugon sa $\\Pi_a^2 = \\Pi_a.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In general, if $\\rho$ is a convex combination\n"
msgstr "Sa pangkalahatan, kung ang $\\rho$ ay isang convex combination\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"of pure states, then the expression $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$ "
"coincides with the average probability for the outcome $a,$ owing to the "
"fact that this expression is linear in $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"ng mga pure state, ang expression na $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$ ay "
"naaayon sa average na probabilidad para sa resulta na $a,$ dahil sa "
"katotohanang ang expression na ito ay linear sa $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\|^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\|^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "General measurements {#general-measurements}"
msgstr "Mga pangkalahatang sukat {#general-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A mathematical description for general measurements is obtained by relaxing the definition of projective measurements.\n"
"Specifically, we allow the matrices in the collection describing the measurement to be arbitrary *positive semidefinite* matrices rather than projections.\n"
"(Projections are always positive semidefinite; they can alternatively be defined as positive semidefinite matrices whose eigenvalues are all either 0 or 1.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang matematikal na paglalarawan para sa mga pangkalahatang sukat ay nakukuha sa pamamagitan ng pagpapaluwag ng kahulugan ng mga projective na sukat.\n"
"Partikular, pinapayagan natin ang mga matris sa koleksyon na nagpapaliwanag ng sukat na maging arbitraryong *positive semidefinite* na mga matris sa halip na mga projection.\n"
"(Ang mga projection ay palaging positive semidefinite; maaari rin silang tukuyin bilang mga positive semidefinite na matris na ang mga eigenvalue ay lahat ay 0 o 1.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, a general measurement of a system $\\mathsf{X}$ having "
"outcomes $0,\\ldots,m-1$ is specified by a collection of positive "
"semidefinite matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ whose rows and columns "
"correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and that meet the "
"condition\n"
msgstr ""
"Partikular, ang isang pangkalahatang sukat ng isang sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ na"
" may mga resulta na $0,\\ldots,m-1$ ay tinukoy ng isang koleksyon ng mga "
"positive semidefinite na matris $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ na ang mga row "
"at column ay naaayon sa mga klasikal na estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ at "
"nakakatugon sa kondisyon\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is measured while it is in a state described by the density matrix $\\rho,$ then each outcome\n"
"$a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ appears with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ ay sinukat habang ito ay nasa isang estado na inilarawan ng density matrix na $\\rho,$ ang bawat resulta\n"
"$a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ ay lumilitaw nang may probabilidad na $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "As we must naturally demand, the vector of outcome probabilities\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng natural na inaasahan, ang vector ng mga probabilidad ng resulta\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho),\\ldots,\\operatorname{Tr}(P_{m-1} \\rho)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho),\\ldots,\\operatorname{Tr}(P_{m-1} \\rho)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"of a general measurement always forms a probability vector, for any choice of a density matrix $\\rho.$\n"
"The following two observations establish that this is the case.\n"
msgstr ""
"ng isang pangkalahatang sukat ay palaging bumubuo ng isang probability vector, para sa anumang pagpili ng density matrix na $\\rho.$\n"
"Ang sumusunod na dalawang obserbasyon ay nagpapatunay na ito ang kaso.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each value $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$ must be nonnegative, owing to the"
" fact that the trace of the product of any two positive semidefinite "
"matrices is always nonnegative:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bawat halaga na $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$ ay dapat na hindi "
"negatibo, dahil sa katotohanang ang trace ng produkto ng anumang dalawang "
"positive semidefinite na matris ay palaging hindi negatibo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   Q, R \\geq 0 \\; \\Rightarrow \\: \\operatorname{Tr}(QR) \\geq 0.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   Q, R \\geq 0 \\; \\Rightarrow \\: \\operatorname{Tr}(QR) \\geq 0.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   One way to argue this fact is to use spectral decompositions of $Q$ and "
"$R$ together with the cyclic property of the trace to express the trace of "
"the product $QR$ as a sum of nonnegative real numbers, which must therefore "
"be nonnegative.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Isang paraan upang patunayan ang katotohanang ito ay ang paggamit ng mga "
"spectral decomposition ng $Q$ at $R$ kasama ang cyclic property ng trace "
"upang ipahayag ang trace ng produkto na $QR$ bilang isang kabuuan ng mga "
"hindi negatibong tunay na bilang, na samakatuwid ay hindi negatibo.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The condition $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ together"
" with the linearity of the trace ensures that the probabilities sum to "
"$1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang kondisyon na $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ "
"kasama ng linearity ng trace ay tinitiyak na ang kabuuan ng mga probabilidad"
" ay $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}\\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a \\rho\\Biggr)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\mathbb{I}\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}\\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a \\rho\\Biggr)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\mathbb{I}\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example 1: any projective measurement {#example-1-any-projective-"
"measurement}"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa 1: anumang projective na sukat {#example-1-any-projective-"
"measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Projections are always positive semidefinite, so every projective "
"measurement is an example of a general measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga projection ay palaging positive semidefinite, kaya ang bawat "
"projective na sukat ay isang halimbawa ng isang pangkalahatang sukat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, a standard basis measurement of a qubit can be represented by "
"$\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa, ang isang standard basis measurement ng isang qubit ay maaaring "
"katawanin ng $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ kung saan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"P_1 = \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{at}\\quad\n"
"P_1 = \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measuring a qubit in the state $\\rho$ results in outcome probabilities as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagsukat ng isang qubit sa estado na $\\rho$ ay nagdudulot ng mga "
"probabilidad ng resulta tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 0)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 0\\vert \\rho \\vert 0 \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 1)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 1 \\vert \\rho \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{resulta} = 0)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 0\\vert \\rho \\vert 0 \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{resulta} = 1)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 1 \\vert \\rho \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example 2: a non-projective qubit measurement {#example-2-a-non-projective-"
"qubit-measurement}"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa 2: isang hindi projective na sukat ng qubit {#example-2-a-non-"
"projective-qubit-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a qubit, and define two matrices as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na ang $\\mathsf{X}$ ay isang qubit, at tukuyin ang dalawang "
"matris tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"P_1 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"P_1 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These are both positive semidefinite matrices: they're Hermitian, and in both cases the eigenvalues happen to be $1/2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}/6,$ which are both positive.\n"
"We also have that $P_0 + P_1 = \\mathbb{I},$ and therefore $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ describes a measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang dalawa ay kapwa positive semidefinite na matris: sila ay Hermitian, at sa parehong kaso ang mga eigenvalue ay $1/2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}/6,$ na kapwa positibo.\n"
"Mayroon din tayong $P_0 + P_1 = \\mathbb{I},$ at samakatuwid ang $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ ay naglalarawan ng isang sukat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is described by a density matrix $\\rho$ and we perform this measurement, then the probability of obtaining the outcome $0$ is $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)$ and the probability of obtaining the outcome $1$ is\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho).$\n"
"For instance, if $\\rho = \\vert + \\rangle \\langle + \\vert$ then the probabilities for the two outcomes $0$ and $1$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ ay inilarawan ng isang density matrix na $\\rho$ at ginagawa natin ang sukat na ito, ang probabilidad na makuha ang resulta na $0$ ay $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)$ at ang probabilidad na makuha ang resulta na $1$ ay\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho).$\n"
"Halimbawa, kung ang $\\rho = \\vert + \\rangle \\langle + \\vert$ ang mga probabilidad para sa dalawang resulta na $0$ at $1$ ay tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{6}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = 0 + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{6}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{6}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = 0 + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{6}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example 3: tetrahedral measurement {#example-3-tetrahedral-measurement}"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa 3: tetrahedral na sukat {#example-3-tetrahedral-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Define four single-qubit quantum state vectors as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tukuyin ang apat na single-qubit na quantum state vector tulad ng "
"sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle & = \\vert 0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_2\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_3\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{-2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle & = \\vert 0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_2\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_3\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{-2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These four states are sometimes known as *tetrahedral* states because "
"they're vertices of a *regular tetrahedron* inscribed within the Bloch "
"sphere.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang apat na estadong ito ay kilala minsan bilang mga *tetrahedral* na estado"
" dahil sila ay mga vertex ng isang *regular na tetrahedron* na nakasulat sa "
"loob ng Bloch sphere.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Illustration of a tetrahedron inscribed in the Bloch "
"sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/general-measurements/tetrahedral-states.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Illustration of a tetrahedron inscribed in the Bloch "
"sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/general-measurements/tetrahedral-states.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Cartesian coordinates of these four states on the Bloch sphere are\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga Cartesian na koordinado ng apat na estadong ito sa Bloch sphere ay\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(0,0,1),\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\left( \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} , 0 , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , -\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(0,0,1),\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\left( \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} , 0 , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , -\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which can be verified by expressing the density matrices representations of "
"these states as linear combinations of Pauli matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"na maaaring mapatunayan sa pamamagitan ng pagpapahayag ng mga "
"representasyong density matrix ng mga estadong ito bilang mga linear na "
"kumbinasyon ng mga Pauli matrix.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_0 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_0 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_0 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_0 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_1 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_1 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_2 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_2 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_3 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_3 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_3 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_3 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These four states are perfectly spread out on the Bloch sphere, each one "
"equidistant from the other three and with the angles between any two of them"
" always being the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang apat na estadong ito ay perpektong nakakalat sa Bloch sphere, ang bawat "
"isa ay pantay na distansya mula sa iba pang tatlo at ang mga anggulo sa "
"pagitan ng anumang dalawa sa kanila ay palaging pareho.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let us define a measurement $\\{P_0,P_1,P_2,P_3\\}$ of a qubit by "
"setting $P_a$ as follows for each $a=0,\\ldots,3.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon tukuyin natin ang isang sukat na $\\{P_0,P_1,P_2,P_3\\}$ ng isang "
"qubit sa pamamagitan ng pagtatakda ng $P_a$ tulad ng sumusunod para sa bawat"
" $a=0,\\ldots,3.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\frac{\\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\frac{\\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can verify that this is a valid measurement as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating patunayan na ito ay isang wastong sukat tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each $P_a$ is evidently positive semidefinite, being a pure state divided by one-half.\n"
"That is, each one is a Hermitian matrix and has one eigenvalue equal to $1/2$ and all other eigenvalues zero.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bawat $P_a$ ay maliwanag na positive semidefinite, dahil ito ay isang pure state na hinati ng isang-kalahati.\n"
"Ibig sabihin, ang bawat isa ay isang Hermitian na matris at may isang eigenvalue na katumbas ng $1/2$ at lahat ng iba pang eigenvalue ay zero.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The sum of these matrices is the identity matrix: $P_0 + P_1 + P_2 + P_3 = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
"The expressions of these matrices as linear combinations of Pauli matrices makes this straightforward to verify.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang kabuuan ng mga matris na ito ay ang identity matrix: $P_0 + P_1 + P_2 + P_3 = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
"Ang mga pagpapahayag ng mga matris na ito bilang mga linear na kumbinasyon ng mga Pauli matrix ay ginagawang diretso ang pagtunay nito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Measurements as channels {#measurements-as-channels}"
msgstr "Mga sukat bilang mga channel {#measurements-as-channels}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A second way to describe measurements in mathematical terms is as "
"channels.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ikalawang paraan upang ilarawan ang mga sukat sa matematikal na termino "
"ay bilang mga channel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Classical information can be viewed as a special case of quantum information, insofar as we can identify probabilistic states with diagonal density matrices.\n"
"So, in operational terms, we can think about measurements as being channels whose inputs are matrices describing states of whatever system is being measured and whose outputs are *diagonal* density matrices describing the resulting distribution of measurement outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang klasikal na impormasyon ay maaaring tingnan bilang isang espesyal na kaso ng quantum na impormasyon, sa lawak na maaari nating tukuyin ang mga probabilistikong estado sa mga diagonal na density matrix.\n"
"Kaya, sa operasyonal na termino, maaari nating isipin ang mga sukat bilang mga channel na ang mga input ay mga matris na nagpapaliwanag ng mga estado ng anumang sistema na sinusukat at ang mga output ay mga *diagonal* na density matrix na nagpapaliwanag ng nagreresultang distribusyon ng mga resulta ng sukat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll see shortly that any channel having this property can always be written in a simple, canonical form that ties directly to the description of measurements as collections of positive semidefinite matrices.\n"
"Conversely, given an arbitrary measurement as a collection of matrices, there's always a valid channel having the diagonal output property that describes the given measurement as suggested in the previous paragraph.\n"
"Putting these observations together, we find that the two descriptions of general measurements are equivalent.\n"
msgstr ""
"Makikita natin sa lalong madaling panahon na ang anumang channel na may katangiang ito ay palaging maaaring isulat sa isang simple, canonical na anyo na direktang nauugnay sa paglalarawan ng mga sukat bilang mga koleksyon ng mga positive semidefinite na matris.\n"
"Sa kabaligtaran, dahil sa isang arbitrary na sukat bilang isang koleksyon ng mga matris, palaging may wastong channel na may katangiang diagonal output na nagpapaliwanag ng ibinigay na sukat tulad ng iminungkahi sa nakaraang talata.\n"
"Pinagsama-sama ang mga obserbasyon na ito, natuklasan natin na ang dalawang paglalarawan ng mga pangkalahatang sukat ay katumbas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before proceeding further, let's be more precise about the measurement, how "
"we're viewing it as a channel, and what assumptions we're making about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago magpatuloy, maging mas tiyak tayo tungkol sa sukat, kung paano natin "
"ito tinitingnan bilang isang channel, at kung anong mga pagpapalagay ang "
"ating ginagawa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As before, we'll suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is the system to be measured, and that the possible outcomes of the measurement are the integers $0,\\ldots,m-1$ for some positive integer $m.$\n"
"We let $\\mathsf{Y}$ be the system that stores measurement outcomes, so its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ and we represent the measurement as a channel named $\\Phi$ from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Our assumption is that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is *classical* — which is to say that no matter what state we start with for $\\mathsf{X},$ the state of $\\mathsf{Y}$ we obtain is represented by a diagonal density matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng dati, ipagpalagay natin na ang $\\mathsf{X}$ ay ang sistema na susukatin, at ang mga posibleng resulta ng sukat ay mga integer na $0,\\ldots,m-1$ para sa ilang positibong integer na $m.$\n"
"Hayaan nating ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ ang sistema na nag-iimbak ng mga resulta ng sukat, kaya ang klasikal na set ng estado nito ay $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ at ikinakategorya natin ang sukat bilang isang channel na pinangalanang $\\Phi$ mula sa $\\mathsf{X}$ patungong $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Ang ating pagpapalagay ay ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay *klasikal* — ibig sabihin, gaano man ang estado na sinimulan natin para sa $\\mathsf{X},$ ang estado ng $\\mathsf{Y}$ na ating nakuha ay kinakatawan ng isang diagonal na density matrix.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can express in mathematical terms that the output of $\\Phi$ is always diagonal in the following way.\n"
"First define the completely dephasing channel $\\Delta_m$ on $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating ipahayag sa matematikal na termino na ang output ng $\\Phi$ ay palaging diagonal sa sumusunod na paraan.\n"
"Una, tukuyin ang completely dephasing channel na $\\Delta_m$ sa $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta_m(\\sigma) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\sigma \\vert a\\rangle \\,\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta_m(\\sigma) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\sigma \\vert a\\rangle \\,\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This channel is analogous to the completely dephasing qubit channel $\\Delta$ from the previous lesson.\n"
"As a linear mapping, it zeros out all of the off-diagonal entries of an input matrix and leaves the diagonal alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang channel na ito ay katulad ng completely dephasing qubit channel na $\\Delta$ mula sa nakaraang aralin.\n"
"Bilang isang linear na mapping, ito ay nagtatanggal ng lahat ng off-diagonal na entry ng isang input matrix at iniiwanan ang diagonal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now, a simple way to express that a given density matrix $\\sigma$ is diagonal is by the equation\n"
"$\\sigma = \\Delta_m(\\sigma).$\n"
"In words, zeroing out all of the off-diagonal entries of a density matrix has no effect if and only if the off-diagonal entries were all zero to begin with.\n"
"The channel $\\Phi$ therefore satisfies our assumption — that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is classical — if and only if\n"
msgstr ""
"At ngayon, isang simpleng paraan upang ipahayag na ang isang ibinigay na density matrix na $\\sigma$ ay diagonal ay sa pamamagitan ng equation na\n"
"$\\sigma = \\Delta_m(\\sigma).$\n"
"Sa salita, ang pagtatanggal ng lahat ng off-diagonal na entry ng isang density matrix ay walang epekto kung at kung lamang ang mga off-diagonal na entry ay zero na sa simula pa lang.\n"
"Ang channel na $\\Phi$ ay samakatuwid ay nakakatugon sa ating pagpapalagay — na ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay klasikal — kung at kung\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\Delta_m(\\Phi(\\rho))\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\Delta_m(\\Phi(\\rho))\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for every density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa bawat density matrix na $\\rho$ na kumakatawan sa isang estado ng "
"$\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalence of the formulations {#equivalence-of-the-formulations}"
msgstr "Katumbasan ng mga pormulasyon {#equivalence-of-the-formulations}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Channels to matrices {#channels-to-matrices}"
msgstr "Mula sa mga channel patungong mga matris {#channels-to-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$ with the "
"property that\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na mayroon tayong isang channel mula sa $\\mathsf{X}$ patungong "
"$\\mathsf{Y}$ na may katangian na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for every density matrix $\\rho.$\n"
"This may alternatively be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa bawat density matrix na $\\rho.$\n"
"Maaari rin itong ipahayag tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Like all channels, we can express $\\Phi$ in Kraus form for some way of choosing Kraus matrices\n"
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng lahat ng channel, maaari nating ipahayag ang $\\Phi$ sa Kraus form para sa ilang paraan ng pagpili ng mga Kraus matrix\n"
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This provides us with an alternative expression for the diagonal entries of "
"$\\Phi(\\rho)\\!:$\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay ito sa atin ng alternatibong expression para sa mga diagonal na "
"entry ng $\\Phi(\\rho)\\!:$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(P_a\\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(P_a\\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "para sa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, for these same matrices $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ we can express the "
"channel $\\Phi$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, para sa mga parehong matris na $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ maaari nating "
"ipahayag ang channel na $\\Phi$ tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This expression is consistent with our description of general measurements "
"in terms of matrices, as we see each measurement outcome appearing with "
"probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang expression na ito ay naaayon sa ating paglalarawan ng mga pangkalahatang"
" sukat sa mga tuntunin ng mga matris, habang nakikita natin ang bawat "
"resulta ng sukat na lumalabas nang may probabilidad na "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's observe that the two properties required of the collection of matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ to describe a general measurement are indeed satisfied.\n"
"The first property is that they're all positive semidefinite matrices.\n"
"One way to see this is to observe that, for every vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ having entries in correspondence with the classical state of $\\mathsf{X}$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay obserbahan natin na ang dalawang katangian na kinakailangan ng koleksyon ng mga matris na $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ para mailarawan ang isang pangkalahatang sukat ay katotohanan na natutupad.\n"
"Ang unang katangian ay ang lahat ng ito ay mga positive semidefinite na matris.\n"
"Isang paraan upang makita ito ay ang pag-obserba na, para sa bawat vector na $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ na may mga entry na naaayon sa klasikal na estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert P_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle \\psi \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"=  \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\bigl\\vert\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\vert^2 \\geq 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert P_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle \\psi \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"=  \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\bigl\\vert\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\vert^2 \\geq 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second property is that if we sum these matrices we get the identity "
"matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ikalawang katangian ay kung i-sum natin ang mga matris na ito makukuha "
"natin ang identity matrix.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\Biggr) A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\Biggr) A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last equality follows from the fact that $\\Phi$ is a channel, so its "
"Kraus matrices must satisfy this condition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang huling pagkakapantay ay sumusunod sa katotohanang ang $\\Phi$ ay isang "
"channel, kaya ang mga Kraus matrix nito ay dapat matupad ang kondisyong "
"ito.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Matrices to channels {#matrices-to-channels}"
msgstr "Mula sa mga matris patungong mga channel {#matrices-to-channels}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's verify that for any collection $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ of "
"positive semidefinite matrices satisfying $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = "
"\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},$ the mapping defined by\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon patunayan natin na para sa anumang koleksyon na "
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ ng mga positive semidefinite na matris na "
"nakakatugon sa $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},$ ang "
"mapping na tinukoy ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is indeed a valid channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"ay katotohanan na isang wastong channel mula sa $\\mathsf{X}$ patungong "
"$\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to do this is to compute the Choi representation of this mapping.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang paraan upang gawin ito ay ang pag-compute ng Choi representation ng "
"mapping na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Phi) & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes \\Phi(\\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Phi) & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes \\Phi(\\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The transpose of each $P_a$ is introduced for the third equality because\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang transpose ng bawat $P_a$ ay ipinakilala para sa ikatlong pagkakapantay "
"dahil\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle c \\vert P_a \\vert b\\rangle = \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle c \\vert P_a \\vert b\\rangle = \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This allows for the expressions $\\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert$ and "
"$\\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert$ to appear, which simplify to the "
"identity matrix upon summing over $b$ and $c,$ respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay nagpapahintulot na lumabas ang mga expression na $\\vert b \\rangle "
"\\langle b \\vert$ at $\\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert,$ na "
"nagpapasimple sa identity matrix kapag sinu-sum sa $b$ at $c,$ ayon sa "
"pagkakasunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the assumption that $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ are positive semidefinite, so too are $P_0^{T},\\ldots,P_{m-1}^{T}.$\n"
"In particular, transposing a Hermitian matrix results in another Hermitian matrix, and the eigenvalues of any square matrix and its transpose always agree.\n"
"It follows that $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite.\n"
"Tracing out the output system $\\mathsf{Y}$ (which is the system on the right) yields\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pamamagitan ng pagpapalagay na ang $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ ay positive semidefinite, gayon din ang $P_0^{T},\\ldots,P_{m-1}^{T}.$\n"
"Partikular, ang pag-transpose ng isang Hermitian na matris ay nagresulta sa isa pang Hermitian na matris, at ang mga eigenvalue ng anumang square matrix at ng transpose nito ay palaging nagtatugma.\n"
"Sumusunod na ang $J(\\Phi)$ ay positive semidefinite.\n"
"Ang pag-trace out ng output system na $\\mathsf{Y}$ (ang sistema sa kanan) ay nagbubunga ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and so we conclude that $\\Phi$ is a channel.\n"
msgstr "at kaya naman napagpasyahan natin na ang $\\Phi$ ay isang channel.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Partial measurements {#partial-measurements}"
msgstr "Mga bahagyang sukat {#partial-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have multiple systems that are collectively in a quantum state, and a general measurement is performed on one of the systems.\n"
"This results in one of the measurement outcomes, selected at random according to probabilities determined by the measurement and the state of the system prior to the measurement.\n"
"The resulting state of the remaining systems will then, in general, depend on which measurement outcome was obtained.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na mayroon tayong maraming sistema na magkasamang nasa isang quantum na estado, at ang isang pangkalahatang sukat ay ginagawa sa isa sa mga sistema.\n"
"Nagdudulot ito ng isa sa mga resulta ng sukat, pinili nang random ayon sa mga probabilidad na tinutukoy ng sukat at ng estado ng sistema bago ang sukat.\n"
"Ang nagreresultang estado ng mga natitirang sistema ay, sa pangkalahatan, ay depende sa kung aling resulta ng sukat ang nakuha.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's examine how this works for a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ when the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is measured.\n"
"(We're naming the system on the right $\\mathsf{Z}$ because we'll take $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be a system representing the classical output of the measurement when we view it as a channel.)\n"
"We can then easily generalize to the situation in which the systems are swapped as well as to three or more systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Suriin natin kung paano ito gumagana para sa isang pares ng mga sistema $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ kapag ang sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ ay sinukat.\n"
"(Pinangalanan natin ang sistema sa kanan na $\\mathsf{Z}$ dahil kukunin natin ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ bilang isang sistema na kumakatawan sa klasikal na output ng sukat kapag tiningnan natin ito bilang isang channel.)\n"
"Maaari nating madaling i-generalize ito sa sitwasyon kung saan ang mga sistema ay naka-swap pati na rin sa tatlo o higit pang sistema.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ prior to the measurement is"
" described by a density matrix $\\rho,$ which we can write as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na ang estado ng $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ bago ang sukat ay "
"inilarawan ng isang density matrix na $\\rho,$ na maaari nating isulat tulad"
" ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this expression we're assuming the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ are "
"$0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa expression na ito ipinagpapalagay natin na ang mga klasikal na estado ng "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ ay $0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll assume that the measurement itself is described by the collection of matrices\n"
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}.$\n"
"This measurement may alternatively be described as a channel $\\Phi$ from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y},$ where $\\mathsf{Y}$ is a new system having classical state set $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"
"Specifically, the action of this channel can be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay natin na ang sukat mismo ay inilarawan ng koleksyon ng mga matris\n"
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}.$\n"
"Ang sukat na ito ay maaari ring ilarawan bilang isang channel na $\\Phi$ mula sa $\\mathsf{X}$ patungong $\\mathsf{Y},$ kung saan ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay isang bagong sistema na may klasikal na set ng estado na $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"
"Partikular, ang aksyon ng channel na ito ay maaaring ipahayag tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\xi) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\xi)\\, \\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\xi) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\xi)\\, \\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Outcome probabilities {#outcome-probabilities}"
msgstr "Mga probabilidad ng resulta {#outcome-probabilities}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We're considering a measurement of the system $\\mathsf{X},$ so the probabilities with which different measurement outcomes are obtained can depend only on $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}},$ the reduced state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"In particular, the probability for each outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ to appear can be expressed in three equivalent ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isinasaalang-alang natin ang isang sukat ng sistema $\\mathsf{X},$ kaya ang mga probabilidad kung saan nakukuha ang iba't ibang resulta ng sukat ay maaaring depende lamang sa $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}},$ ang reduced na estado ng $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Partikular, ang probabilidad para sa bawat resulta na $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ na lumabas ay maaaring ipahayag sa tatlong katumbas na paraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( (P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( (P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first expression naturally represents the probability to obtain the outcome $a$ based on what we already know about measurements of a single system.\n"
"To get the second expression we're simply using the definition $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang expression ay natural na kumakatawan sa probabilidad na makuha ang resulta na $a$ batay sa kung ano na ang alam natin tungkol sa mga sukat ng isang sistema.\n"
"Para makuha ang ikalawang expression, ginagamit natin lamang ang kahulugan na $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To get the third expression requires more thought — and learners are encouraged to convince themselves that it is true.\n"
"Here's a hint: The equivalence between the second and third expressions does not depend on $\\rho$ being a density matrix or on each $P_a$ being positive semidefinite. Try showing it first for tensor products of the form $\\rho = M\\otimes N$ and then conclude that it must be true in general by linearity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para makuha ang ikatlong expression ay nangangailangan ng mas malalim na pag-iisip — at hinihikayat ang mga mag-aaral na kumbinsihin ang kanilang sarili na ito ay totoo.\n"
"Narito ang isang pahiwatig: Ang katumbasan sa pagitan ng ikalawa at ikatlong expression ay hindi depende sa $\\rho$ na isang density matrix o sa bawat $P_a$ na positive semidefinite. Subukang ipakita ito muna para sa mga tensor product na may anyo $\\rho = M\\otimes N$ at pagkatapos ay tapusin na ito ay totoo sa pangkalahatan sa pamamagitan ng linearity.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the equivalence of the first and third expressions in the previous equation may not be immediate, it does make sense.\n"
"Starting from a measurement on $\\mathsf{X},$ we're effectively defining a measurement of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z}),$ where we simply throw away $\\mathsf{Z}$ and measure $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Like all measurements, this new measurement can be described by a collection of matrices, and it's not surprising that this measurement is described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Kahit hindi agad na malinaw ang katumbasan ng una at ikatlong expression sa nakaraang equation, ito ay may katuturan.\n"
"Simula sa isang sukat sa $\\mathsf{X},$ epektibo tayong nagtatakda ng isang sukat ng $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z}),$ kung saan itinapon lang natin ang $\\mathsf{Z}$ at sinusukat ang $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Gaya ng lahat ng sukat, ang bagong sukat na ito ay maaaring ilarawan ng isang koleksyon ng mga matris, at hindi nakakagulat na ang sukat na ito ay inilarawan ng koleksyon\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{P_0\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}, \\ldots, P_{m-1}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{P_0\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}, \\ldots, P_{m-1}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"States conditioned on measurement outcomes {#states-conditioned-on-"
"measurement-outcomes}"
msgstr ""
"Mga estado na nakondisyon sa mga resulta ng sukat {#states-conditioned-on-"
"measurement-outcomes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we want to determine not only the probabilities for the different outcomes but also the resulting state of $\\mathsf{Z}$ conditioned on each measurement outcome, we can look to the channel description of the measurement.\n"
"In particular, let's examine the state we get when we apply $\\Phi$ to $\\mathsf{X}$ and do nothing to $\\mathsf{Z}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung gusto nating matukoy hindi lamang ang mga probabilidad para sa iba't ibang resulta kundi pati na rin ang nagreresultang estado ng $\\mathsf{Z}$ na nakondisyon sa bawat resulta ng sukat, maaari tayong tumingin sa channel na paglalarawan ng sukat.\n"
"Partikular, suriin natin ang estado na nakukuha natin kapag inilapat natin ang $\\Phi$ sa $\\mathsf{X}$ at walang ginagawa sa $\\mathsf{Z}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  (\\Phi\\otimes\\operatorname{Id}_{\\mathsf{Z}})(\\rho)\n"
"  & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\Phi(\\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert)\n"
"    \\,\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1}\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}})\n"
"    (\\vert b\\rangle\\langle  c\\vert\\otimes\\rho_{b,c})\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  (\\Phi\\otimes\\operatorname{Id}_{\\mathsf{Z}})(\\rho)\n"
"  & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\Phi(\\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert)\n"
"    \\,\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1}\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}})\n"
"    (\\vert b\\rangle\\langle  c\\vert\\otimes\\rho_{b,c})\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this is a density matrix by virtue of the fact that $\\Phi$ is a channel, so each matrix\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$ is necessarily positive semidefinite.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ito ay isang density matrix dahil sa katotohanang ang $\\Phi$ ay isang channel, kaya ang bawat matris na\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$ ay kinakailangang positive semidefinite.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One final step transforms this expression into one that reveals what we're "
"looking for.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang huling hakbang ay nag-transform ng expression na ito sa isa na "
"nagpapakita ng hinahanap natin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is an example of a *classical-quantum state*,\n"
msgstr "Ito ay isang halimbawa ng isang *classical-quantum state*,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} p(a)\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert \\otimes \\sigma_a,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} p(a)\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert \\otimes \\sigma_a,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"like we saw in the *Density matrices* lesson.\n"
"For each measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ we have with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"gaya ng nakita natin sa aralin na *Density matrices*.\n"
"Para sa bawat resulta ng sukat na $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ mayroon tayong may probabilidad na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is in the classical state $\\vert a \\rangle \\langle a "
"\\vert$ and $\\mathsf{Z}$ is in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"na ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay nasa klasikal na estado na $\\vert a \\rangle "
"\\langle a \\vert$ at ang $\\mathsf{Z}$ ay nasa estado na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_a = \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_a = \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "That is, this is the density matrix we obtain by normalizing\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibig sabihin, ito ang density matrix na nakukuha natin sa pamamagitan ng "
"pag-normalize ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"by dividing it by its trace.\n"
"(Formally speaking, the state $\\sigma_a$ is only defined when the probability $p(a)$ is nonzero;\n"
"when $p(a) = 0$ this state is irrelevant, for it refers to a discrete event that occurs with probability zero.)\n"
msgstr ""
"sa pamamagitan ng paghati nito sa trace nito.\n"
"(Sa pormal na pagsasalita, ang estado na $\\sigma_a$ ay tinukoy lamang kapag ang probabilidad na $p(a)$ ay hindi zero;\n"
"kapag ang $p(a) = 0$ ang estadong ito ay walang kaugnayan, dahil tumutukoy ito sa isang discrete na pangyayari na nangyayari nang may probabilidad na zero.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Naturally, the outcome probabilities are consistent with our previous "
"observations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Natural na, ang mga probabilidad ng resulta ay naaayon sa ating mga "
"nakaraang obserbasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In summary, this is what happens when the measurement "
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ is performed on $\\mathsf{X}$ when "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ is in the state $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa buod, ito ang nangyayari kapag ang sukat na $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ "
"ay ginagawa sa $\\mathsf{X}$ kapag ang $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ ay nasa "
"estado na $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each outcome $a$ appears with probability $p(a) = "
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bawat resulta na $a$ ay lumilitaw nang may probabilidad na $p(a) = "
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho).$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Conditioned on obtaining the outcome $a,$ the state of $\\mathsf{Z}$ is then"
" represented by the density matrix $\\sigma_a$ shown in the equation $(2),$ "
"which is obtained by normalizing "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes "
"\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakondisyon sa pagkuha ng resulta na $a,$ ang estado ng $\\mathsf{Z}$ ay "
"kinakatawan ng density matrix na $\\sigma_a$ na ipinapakita sa equation na "
"$(2),$ na nakukuha sa pamamagitan ng pag-normalize ng "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes "
"\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho).$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generalization {#generalization}"
msgstr "Generalisasyon {#generalization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can adapt this description to other situations, such as when the ordering of the systems is reversed or when there are three or more systems.\n"
"Conceptually it is straightforward, although it can become cumbersome to write down the formulas.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating iakma ang paglalarawang ito sa ibang mga sitwasyon, tulad ng kapag ang pagkakasunod ng mga sistema ay binaliktad o kapag mayroong tatlo o higit pang mga sistema.\n"
"Konseptwal ito ay diretso, kahit maaaring maging mabigat ang pagsulat ng mga formula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, if we have $r$ systems $\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r,$ "
"the state of the compound system $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ is "
"$\\rho,$ and the measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ is performed on "
"$\\mathsf{X}_k$, the following happens.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pangkalahatan, kung mayroon tayong $r$ na mga sistema "
"$\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r,$ ang estado ng compound system na "
"$(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ ay $\\rho,$ at ang sukat na "
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ ay ginagawa sa $\\mathsf{X}_k$, ang sumusunod ay"
" nangyayari.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each outcome $a$ appears with probability\n"
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bawat resulta na $a$ ay lumilitaw nang may probabilidad na\n"
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Conditioned on obtaining the outcome $a,$ the state of $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_{k-1},\\mathsf{X}_{k+1},\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ is then represented by the following density matrix.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}_k}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakondisyon sa pagkuha ng resulta na $a,$ ang estado ng $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_{k-1},\\mathsf{X}_{k+1},\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ ay kinakatawan ng sumusunod na density matrix.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}_k}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}\n"
"$$\n"
